.TH VECTORCRAFT 1 "November 2026" "VectorCraft 0.24.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vectorcraft \- open-source vector illustration editor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vectorcraft
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ file ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vectorcraft
starts VectorCraft, a native vector illustration app written in Rust. It has pen, shape and brush tools, artboards,
type, gradients, symbols and live effects, and opens and saves SVG and PDF. Files given on the command line are
opened as tabs, in the running window when VectorCraft is already running.
.PP
Headless work (converting, running commands, the MCP server) is done by
.BR vectorcraft-cli (1).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-safe\-mode
Start without plug-ins: none loads or runs. Plug-ins stay installed.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the list of all options and exit.
.PP
.B vectorcraft \-\-help
lists the remaining options, such as
.B \-\-new\-instance
and
.BR "\-\-control PORT" ,
which lets
.B "vectorcraft-cli mcp"
attach to the running window.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/vectorcraft/
Settings (\fIui.json\fR), the user's swatches, graphic styles and fonts, data recovery files and logs.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vectorcraft-cli (1)
.PP
https://getartcraft.com/apps/vectorcraft
